---
title: Kung Pao Chicken
source: https://www.theguardian.com/food/2020/feb/19/how-to-make-the-perfect-kung-pao-gong-bao-chicken-recipe
servings: 1
course: Main
prep time: 15m
cook time: 15m
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Chinese
---

= Marinade Chicken =

Mix the @cornflour{1%tsp} and @cold water{1%tsp} to make a rough paste. Stir in the @light soy sauce{0.5%tsp} and @dry sherry{0.5%tsp}. Add the @chicken, skinless{1%breast}(cut into 1cm cubes) and toss to coat.

= Sauce =

Mix all of the ingredients for the sauce: @sugar{1%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{0.5tsp}, @light soy sauce{0.75%tsp}, @vinegar{1%tbsp}, and @cornflour{0.5%tsp}.

= Fry =

Heat a #wok, add the @sunflower oil{1.5%tbsp}, @Sichuan peppercorns, whole{1%tsp}, and @dried chillies{6}(cut in half lengthways and seeds discarded). Stir-fry until aromatic.

Add the chicken and fry until just coloured all-over.

Add the @garlic{2%cloves}(thinly sliced), @fresh ginger{2%cm}(thinly sliced), and @spring onions{3}(cut into 1 cm chunks, greens and whites separated) whites. Cook until the chicken is just cooked-through. Keep everything moving to prevent the garlic from burning.

Whisk the sauce and add to the wok. Leave it to bubble until thickened sufficiently to coat the chicken.

Add the @cashews (or peanuts){30%g} and spring onion greens. Toss everything together. Serve immediately with @rice.